{"id":"u-82b5c5fb-b235-44b0-8745-097e1c372a71","src":"community","title":"Tactical Athlete V2","author":"Brian Z.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/TJ6mG0-tactical-athlete-v2","desc":"The three lifting sessions are only the strength component of a complete tactical-athlete program. On non-lifting days, athletes should add conditioning according to their individual goals and recovery.\n\nUtilize double progression with all exercises, but try to stick with prescribed RPEs.\n\nA well-rounded week can include:\n\n1 easy aerobic session: 30–60 minutes of easy running, cycling, swimming, or similar Zone 2 work.\n1 quality running session: intervals, hills, tempo/threshold work, or other goal-specific conditioning.\n1 optional conditioning session: rucking, sandbag training, loaded carries, recreational sports, or additional easy aerobic work.\nAt least 1 recovery day each week.\n\nYou can choose to prioritize different aspects of the program such as:\n-Skipping a lifting session for conditioning\n-Skipping a run/conditioning session to lift\n-Skip some exercises if a specific muscle group is not well recovered\n\nThe purpose of this program is modularity to the user's goals. It is not expected or recommended to be able to successfully complete every single session every week, but to tailor the program to your personal goals. If you have the work capacity and recovery dialed in enough to do everything, then do it.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-15T08:27:02.897Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Squat + Upper","Hinge + Upper","Full Body"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Broad Jump","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":8},{"lo":5,"hi":6,"rpe":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":6,"rpe":8},{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":6,"x":2}],"note":"Substitute for weighted pushups if needed."},{"n":"Pull-